---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/asbj/implementation-guidance-overview.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope – Where Implementation Guidance Sits Within ASBJ's Output" },
        { id: "s3", label: "What Implementation Guidance Actually Contains" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Numbering – Independent From, and Not Aligned With, Statement Numbers" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Confirmed Guidance-to-Statement Mapping Encountered in This Series" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Revisions – Guidance Is Updated as Its Companion Statement Evolves" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Distinguishing Implementation Guidance From Practical Solutions" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Worked Example – Using Guidance to Resolve an Application Question" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Worked Example – a Guidance Revision Following a Statement Amendment" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Critical Judgments" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Relationship to IAS/IFRS" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="callout info callout--centered">SCOPE NOTE: Implementation Guidance is numbered independently from ASBJ Statements (see the companion ASBJ Guidance No. 32 poster on this numbering distinction). This poster explains the document type generally and maps the specific Guidance numbers confirmed or referenced elsewhere in this poster series to their companion Statements, rather than producing 30+ near-duplicate individual posters.</div>

    <div class="toc">
      <a href="#s1">1. Conceptual Framework Linkage</a><a href="#s2">2. Scope – Where Implementation Guidance Sits Within ASBJ's Output</a><a href="#s3">3. What Implementation Guidance Actually Contains</a>
      <a href="#s4">4. Numbering – Independent From, and Not Aligned With, Statement Numbers</a><a href="#s5">5. Confirmed Guidance-to-Statement Mapping Encountered in This Series</a>
      <a href="#s6">6. Revisions – Guidance Is Updated as Its Companion Statement Evolves</a><a href="#s7">7. Distinguishing Implementation Guidance From Practical Solutions</a>
      <a href="#s8">8. Worked Example – Using Guidance to Resolve an Application Question</a><a href="#s9">9. Worked Example – a Guidance Revision Following a Statement Amendment</a>
      <a href="#s10">10. Disclosure Requirements</a><a href="#s11">11. Critical Judgments</a>
      <a href="#s12">12. Relationship to IAS/IFRS</a><a href="#s13">13. Statement Mapping</a><a href="#s14">14. Related Standards</a><a href="#s15">15. Glossary</a>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Turning principles into practice</div>
        <div class="principle">"IMPLEMENTATION GUIDANCE" (適用指針) is the ASBJ document TYPE that translates a PRINCIPLES-based Accounting Standard (an ASBJ Statement) into DETAILED, PRACTICAL, application-level guidance – worked scenarios, specific interpretive answers, and illustrative examples helping PREPARERS apply a Statement's requirements CONSISTENTLY. A Statement sets out the PRINCIPLE; its companion Implementation Guidance explains HOW to apply that principle in PRACTICE, across a range of concrete FACT patterns.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope – Where Implementation Guidance Sits Within ASBJ's Output</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">One of several parallel ASBJ document types</div>
        <div class="principle">As ESTABLISHED in the companion ASBJ Guidance No. 32 poster, ASBJ's output spans SEVERAL parallel document types: ACCOUNTING STANDARDS (Statements), IMPLEMENTATION GUIDANCE, PRACTICAL SOLUTIONS (see the companion overview poster), and TRANSFERRED GUIDANCE – EACH numbered INDEPENDENTLY, and EACH playing a DISTINCT structural role.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>What Implementation Guidance Actually Contains</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Worked scenarios, interpretive answers, and illustrative examples</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">A TYPICAL piece of Implementation Guidance contains: ILLUSTRATIVE examples applying the companion Statement's PRINCIPLES to specific fact patterns; ANSWERS to commonly-arising APPLICATION questions; TRANSITION guidance for newly-issued Statements; and, WHERE relevant, PRACTICAL expedients or simplified approaches CONSISTENT with the Statement's OVERALL objectives.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Numbering – Independent From, and Not Aligned With, Statement Numbers</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Guidance No. X does not correspond to Statement No. X</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">CRITICALLY, Guidance numbers do NOT correspond to the SAME number as their companion STATEMENT – Guidance No. 30 supports Statement No. 29 (Revenue Recognition); Guidance No. 33 supports Statement No. 34 (Leases); Guidance No. 34 supports Statement No. 37 (Interim Financial Reporting). The TWO sequences have simply DIVERGED over time as EACH has grown at its OWN pace, making CONTEXT – not the number ALONE – essential for CORRECTLY identifying which Statement a given piece of Guidance supports.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Confirmed Guidance-to-Statement Mapping Encountered in This Series</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">A working reference table</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-06-15-09"><span>Guidance No.</span><span>Title</span><span>Companion Statement</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-06-15-09"><span>No. 2</span><span>Treasury Shares and Appropriation of Legal Reserve</span><span>Statement No. 1</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-06-15-09"><span>No. 6</span><span>Impairment of Fixed Assets</span><span>(Impairment standard)</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-06-15-09"><span>No. 13</span><span>Related Party</span><span>Statement No. 11</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-06-15-09"><span>No. 19</span><span>Disclosures about Fair Value of Financial Instruments</span><span>Statement No. 10</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-06-15-09"><span>No. 28</span><span>Tax Effect Accounting</span><span>Statement No. 28</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-06-15-09"><span>No. 30</span><span>Revenue Recognition</span><span>Statement No. 29</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-06-15-09"><span>No. 32</span><span>Semi-annual Financial Reporting</span><span>Statement No. 33 (superseded)</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-06-15-09"><span>No. 33</span><span>Leases</span><span>Statement No. 34</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-06-15-09"><span>No. 34</span><span>Interim Financial Reporting</span><span>Statement No. 37</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="note">This table reflects Guidance numbers SPECIFICALLY confirmed or referenced elsewhere in THIS poster series – it is NOT a complete enumeration of every Guidance number from 1 through 34+; ASBJ's own current index should be consulted for the FULL, up-to-date list.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Revisions – Guidance Is Updated as Its Companion Statement Evolves</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">Kept in step with the underlying Statement over time</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">WHEN a companion Statement is REVISED (as with the 2026 Financial Instruments and Current Income Taxes amendments – see the companion posters), its Implementation Guidance is TYPICALLY revised IN TANDEM – for example, Guidance No. 28 has been REVISED multiple times (2022, 2024) ALONGSIDE amendments to the underlying Tax Effect Accounting Statement, ensuring the PRACTICAL application guidance stays CURRENT with the principle it supports.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Distinguishing Implementation Guidance From Practical Solutions</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Companion detail vs a standalone narrow answer</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">Implementation Guidance ALWAYS has a SPECIFIC companion Statement it supports – it exists to APPLY that Statement's principles. A PRACTICAL SOLUTION (see the companion overview poster), BY CONTRAST, often stands ALONE, addressing a NARROW question NOT yet covered by ANY existing Statement (e.g. a brand-new tax measure) – it is NOT necessarily tied to a SPECIFIC companion Statement in the SAME way Implementation Guidance is.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example – Using Guidance to Resolve an Application Question</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">Turning a general principle into a specific answer</div>
        <div class="worked worked--flush">
          <div class="wk-title">Example: Applying the Leases Statement to an ambiguous contract</div>
          <div class="wk-body">A company is uncertain whether a specific service contract meets ASBJ Statement No. 34's redefined "lease" criteria (see the companion poster), given the contract's unusual terms.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer">The company consults ASBJ IMPLEMENTATION GUIDANCE No. 33 (the COMPANION guidance to Statement No. 34), which provides ILLUSTRATIVE examples and interpretive ANSWERS addressing SIMILAR borderline scenarios – helping the company reach a CONSISTENT, well-supported conclusion WITHOUT needing to interpret the Statement's general PRINCIPLES entirely from first principles.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example – a Guidance Revision Following a Statement Amendment</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Keeping application guidance current</div>
        <div class="worked worked--flush">
          <div class="wk-title">Example: The 2026 Financial Instruments exposure draft</div>
          <div class="wk-body">Following the ASBJ's February 2026 exposure draft proposing an expected credit loss model for ASBJ Statement No. 10 (see the companion poster), a SEPARATE, dedicated new Implementation Guidance on "Accounting for Expected Credit Losses on Financial Assets" was ALSO released.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer">This ILLUSTRATES the GENERAL pattern: a MAJOR Statement-level change is ACCOMPANIED by CORRESPONDING new or revised Implementation Guidance, providing the PRACTICAL detail (illustrative expected-loss calculations, staging criteria, disclosure examples) preparers NEED to apply the NEW principle consistently.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">What Implementation Guidance typically addresses</div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span>Illustrative worked examples applying the companion Statement's principles</span>
          <span>Answers to commonly arising practical application questions</span>
          <span>Transition guidance for newly issued or revised Statements</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Identifying the correct companion Guidance number for a given Statement, since numbers do not correspond directly</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Varies entirely by the specific companion Statement's subject matter</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">A rough parallel to IFRS Illustrative Examples and Implementation Guidance</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">Internationally, individual IFRS Standards are OFTEN accompanied by their OWN "Illustrative Examples" and "Implementation Guidance" sections, PUBLISHED alongside (though NOT formally PART of) the Standard itself – SERVING a broadly SIMILAR function to ASBJ's Implementation Guidance: translating PRINCIPLES into practical, worked APPLICATION. The KEY structural difference is that ASBJ's Implementation Guidance is a SEPARATELY numbered, standalone DOCUMENT type, WHEREAS IFRS's equivalent material is typically published AS PART of the same Standard's overall package.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Not applicable directly – depends entirely on the companion Statement</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-16-1-14"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Any Guidance-supported event</span><span>Whatever the companion Statement governs</span><span>Guidance itself has no independent measurement effect</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-08-2"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Guidance No. 32</span><span>Illustrates the broader numbering-distinction issue this poster generalises</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-08-2"><span>Practical Solutions (overview)</span><span>The companion, narrower ASBJ document type this poster distinguishes Implementation Guidance from</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Implementation Guidance (適用指針)</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">A separately numbered ASBJ document type providing detailed, practical application guidance for a specific companion Accounting Standard.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item glossary-item--last">
          <div class="glossary-term">Companion Statement</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">The specific ASBJ Statement (Accounting Standard) a given piece of Implementation Guidance is designed to support and apply.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="legend">
      <div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div>
      <div class="lrow">
        <span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (貸借対照表)
        <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書)
        <span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> 純資産の部
        <span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書)
        <span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</StandardPageLayout>
